[B]Soft dependencies (all optional):[/B] PlaceholderAPI, ProtocolLib. [I]PaperLib is no longer required. Vault economy ships in [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B].[/I]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='❓ FAQ']
[B]Q: How do I stop /rtp from lagging my server, and why is LeafRTP faster than other random teleport plugins?[/B]
A: Most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve from a pre-warmed queue — chunks are already loaded and safety-checked before you type the command. Two design choices make that queue cheap to keep full: a [B]persistent spatial memory[/B] per region (the plugin remembers which sectors of the world failed safety checks, so the spiral selector skips known-bad ground instead of rerolling forever), and an [B]off-tick async pre-filter[/B] (Anvil region files are read directly to reject unsafe biomes/blocks [I]before[/I] any chunk is loaded, so candidate verification never blocks the main thread). The pre-warmed queue is just the visible tip — the spatial memory keeps candidate selection bounded, and the async pre-filter keeps verification off the tick loop.

[B]Q: Why is it called "LeafRTP" now instead of just "RTP"?[/B]
A: "RTP" is the generic term for random teleport, so the old name was nearly impossible to find — it collided with every other random-teleport plugin, command, and forum thread in search and marketplace indexes. "LeafRTP" is a distinct, indexable name that points unambiguously at this plugin while keeping the [I]/rtp[/I] command, [I]rtp-api[/I], config paths, and data files exactly as they were. Nothing changes for existing installs — only the public name.

[B]Q: Does it work with Iris / Terra / custom datapack generators?[/B]
A: Yes. Region files are read directly, so modded and namespaced biome and block IDs are preserved. No configuration needed.

[B]Q: What's the difference between LeafRTP and LeafRTP-Pro?[/B]
A: Same engine, same source tree. [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B] adds the Folia adapter, multi-server / proxy support (Velocity), SQL/Redis backends, Vault economy, multilingual [I]lang/**[/I], the richer block-tag/state-predicate [I]safety.yml[/I] grammar, and priority support. The free build is fully sufficient for single-server deployments. Drop in the Pro jar later - same config, same data, same commands.

[B]Q: I'm on Forge / NeoForge.[/B]
A: Run [B]Arclight[/B] or [B]Mohist[/B] (officially supported) and use this jar. A native Forge adapter is not planned.

[B]Q: Memory and MSPT — should I worry?[/B]
A: LeafRTP trades a bounded amount of RAM (the queue, bounded by [I]cacheCap[/I]) for speed. TPS should not drop below ~19 from LeafRTP alone on a healthy server; MSPT spikes during new-area generation are expected — that's the cost of generating chunks, not RTP.

[B]Q: How do I report a bug?[/B]
A: GitHub issue with server version, LeafRTP version, platform, relevant config files, and the error log section. See the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md']admin guide[/URL] for the full reproduction template.
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='📞 Community Support Policy (read before filing an issue)']
Support for the free build is [B]community-tier and best-effort[/B] — a solo maintainer ships fixes when properly-reported issues land. Respecting this is how the plugin stays fast and current.
[LIST]
[*][B]Support covers bugs and configuration questions,[/B] after you've read the admin guide.
[*][B]Bug reports need a reproduction:[/B] server version, LeafRTP version, platform (Spigot / Paper / fork), [I]config.yml[/I], [I]regions/[/I], [I]safety.yml[/I], and the relevant [I]server.log[/I] section. Reports without these are asked for them once, then closed.
[*][B]"It doesn't work" is not a bug report.[/B] Tell me what you did, what you expected, and what actually happened.
[*][B]Unsupported on the free tier:[/B] native Forge / NeoForge (use Arclight / Mohist), plugin conflicts I can't reproduce, general MC-server admin questions.
[*][B]Response time:[/B] no SLA on the free build. Critical safety issues (S-001…S-007 violations) jump the queue regardless. Guaranteed response windows are reserved for [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B].
[*][B]Feature requests[/B] via GitHub issues. Priority follows the published roadmap, not ticket volume.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

[SPOILER='⚠️ Known limitations in 3.0.0-beta.3']
[LIST]
[*]Free build does not ship Folia, SQL/Redis, multi-server, Vault economy, multilingual [I]lang/**[/I], or the tag/state-predicate [I]safety.yml[/I] grammar — all are in [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B].
[*][I]safety.yml[/I] here accepts flat material names ([I]LAVA[/I], [I]MAGMA_BLOCK[/I], [I]CACTUS[/I], [I]FIRE[/I]). Unknown materials log one warning, never silently dropped.
[*]Edits to [I]safety.yml[/I] and biome filters do not yet invalidate the persisted shape cache — workaround: [I]/rtp scan reset <region>[/I].
[*]Emergency landing platform default is now [I]platformRadius: -1[/I] (disabled). Set to [I]0[/I] or higher to restore legacy 2.x behavior.
[/LIST]
Live list: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/CHANGELOG.md#known-issues']CHANGELOG[/URL].
[/SPOILER]

